<title>USA: Louisiana to spend tobacco money on teen programs.</title>
<headline>Louisiana to spend tobacco money on teen programs.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Louisiana Attorney General Richard Ieyoub on Friday said the state expected to use a &quot;large share&quot; of any money it receives from a proposed tobacco settlement on programs to help teen-agers quit smoking.</p>
<p>Ieyoub, speaking to reporters at a news conference in Baton Rouge, said Louisiana expected at least $120 million from the settlement in the first year. That would increase to $200 million a year after the first five years, he said.</p>
</text>
